                <pb facs="0713" n="633" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg633"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to
                        Commander McCrea</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Ignore Killick’s blockade. See that foreign vessels have free entrance to Cape.
                    Act in accordance with these instructions unless instructed otherwise by
                    Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
